{
  "name": "Understanding the Timeline for Your Full Kitchen Remodel",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "So, you're dreaming of a full kitchen remodel, but how long will it actually take? That's a common question, and the answer isn't always simple, as it really depends on the scope. For a complete gut renovation, where you're changing the layout, moving walls, or relocating plumbing and electrical, you're typically looking at a longer timeline, often in the range of 18-20 weeks from start to finish. This timeframe includes everything from initial design and material ordering to demolition, structural work, and the final installation of finishes. Keep in mind that lead times for materials can impact this significantly, so ordering early is key. HH Remodeling LLC, with Abraham as the hands-on general contractor, is skilled at coordinating these complex projects, ensuring all the different stages, including sub-trades like plumbing and electrical, are scheduled efficiently. If your project is less extensive, say a full remodel that doesn't involve major structural changes but still updates everything, some sources suggest around 2.5-3 weeks of total project time, with about 7-10 working days of actual construction. It's important to clarify the exact scope with your contractor to get a realistic timeline. Always discuss payment and warranty terms, and ensure communication expectations are clear from the outset, as HH Remodeling LLC prides itself on open communication.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
